{"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Nexus()"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick"},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}]},{"text":"The sparse-set storage","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The archetype storage","level":3,"anchor":"The-archetype-storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"text":" follows the design of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()"},{"text":" drops all tables.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait (","type":"text"},{"code":"Sparse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","text":"What the numbers say","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass (","type":"text"},{"code":"make benchmark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Benchmarks\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"alignments":["left","right","right"],"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Case"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sparse set"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Archetype","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2.5 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"31 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4.4 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"23 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6.1 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"227 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"27 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 200 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 800 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"455 μs","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Random ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.get"},{"text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"345 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 180 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4 900 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 730 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 510 μs"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two (","type":"text"},{"code":"IterOnlyOneComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating with "},{"code":"forEach(reading:writing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"text":"Which storage to pick","anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet"},{"text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Differences you can observe","anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe","type":"heading","level":3},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration order."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or your own key if you need one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single-type spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Family spans."}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents"},{"text":" for the spans.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Choosing a storage","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"text":", and know what changes.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(writing:_:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"writing","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV","text":"MutableSpan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"}],"title":"componentSpan(writing:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Gives ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" write access to all components of a type as one contiguous ","type":"text"},{"code":"MutableSpan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(writing:_:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A delegate for receiving Nexus events and errors."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventdelegate","title":"NexusEventDelegate","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/init(storage:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/init(storage:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"storage"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Nexus"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO","text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializes a new Nexus."}],"type":"topic","title":"init(storage:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/default":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"`default`"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","text":"Nexus"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO","text":"StorageKind","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The storage "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)"},{"type":"text","text":" uses by default: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/default","role":"symbol","title":"default","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"kind":"article","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReadingAndWritingComponents":{"role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","title":"Reading and writing components","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read a copy, replace a component or change it in place."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/readingandwritingcomponents"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reading"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Span","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Span"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(reading:_:)","title":"componentSpan(reading:_:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEvent"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEvent"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"NexusEvent","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","role":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Benchmarks":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"title":"Benchmarks","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic."}],"title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"topic","abstract":[],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus","title":"Nexus","role":"symbol","fragments"